            <div xml:id="d1049">

                <pb facs="0782" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 125.8273/84b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Brazilian Minister at Mexico City.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. Department would appreciate brief telegraphic statement of charges which
                    were lodged by Huerta Government against Vice Consul Silliman, including
                    information as to whether these charges have now been dismissed. Would
                    Silliman’s return to Saltillo at this time be likely to embarrass you in any
                    way?</p>
                <p>As a matter of record, the Department would be glad to have copies by mail of the
                    notes exchanged by you with the Mexican Foreign Office in regard to Silliman, if
                    not objectionable to you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
